<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Revival Lê dynasty</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1533">1533</a>–<a href="/years/1789">1789</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> · Also known as Later Lê restoration</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Revival Lê dynasty was the restored Lê imperial line of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vietnam">Vietnam</a> from 1533 to 1789. After the Mạc seized the throne in 1527, loyalists under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nguyen-kim">Nguyễn Kim</a> set up a Lê emperor in Thanh Hóa, and this southern court fought the Mạc until it retook <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thang-long">Thăng Long</a> in 1592. Real power lay with the Trịnh lords in the north and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nguyen-lords">Nguyễn lords</a> in the south, and the line ended in 1789 during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tay-son-dynasty">Tây Sơn</a> wars.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/revival-le-dynasty.jpg" alt="Revival Lê dynasty" width="320" height="533" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Created by CGlassey, based on province map of Vietnam. Map data based on &quot;The Empire of Le Thanh-tong&quot; (from Jonh Whi... · CC BY 2.5 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:VietnamMac1540.gif" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
